// std.runtime - R2 Evaluator / PB-Runtime observable runtime values.
//
// This module lands PR-A.1's Value-only carrier surface. It deliberately
// excludes evaluator-internal state (`EvalFrame`, `EvalStateStack`,
// `EvalThunk`) and body-evaluator logic; those land in later PR-A slices.
//
// Authority: docs/design-pb-runtime-interpreter.md section 3.2 and
// docs/briefs/r2-pr-a-runtime-value-model.md. The existing L1 behavior marker
// is `ValueBehavior`, so the bare declaration name `Value` is reserved here for
// the observable runtime result domain.

module v3.std.runtime

import std.list { List }
import std.types { Map }
import v3.std.substrate { Dag, LiteralBits, LitInt, LoopBound }
import v3.std.substrate_minimal { NodeId, PortId, DeclarationId }

type NamedField {
  label: String
  value: Value
}

// 🟢 TERMINAL at PR-A.1 observable-runtime scope. This is the single
// PB-Runtime / R2-Evaluator runtime result-domain carrier locked by
// docs/design-pb-runtime-interpreter.md section 3.2 and
// docs/briefs/r2-pr-a-runtime-value-model.md. The five variants are the
// irreducible inhabitants the evaluator can return or pass as runtime data:
//
//   - `LiteralValue` for Bit / Atom inhabitants through `LiteralBits`
//   - `RecordValue` for Conj inhabitants through `NamedField`
//   - `VariantValue` for Disj inhabitants through declaration-tagged payloads
//   - `NodeRef` for behavior-bearing node identity, not inlined subtrees
//   - `CardinalityValue` for bounded iteration / cardinality inhabitants
//
// `Arrow` and `Instantiation` intentionally are not variants: Arrow values are
// represented structurally through `Bind` / callable node identity plus the
// evaluator's internal frame stack, and instantiation erases to the instantiated
// runtime value. This type must not grow `ClosureValue`; captured environments
// are PR-A.2 evaluator state (`EvalFrame` / `EvalStateStack`), not observable
// `Value`. Dissolution trigger: none until PB-Runtime / PR-A.0 is explicitly
// amended through the substrate-fact-introduction path; this carrier is the
// convergence authority, not a scaffold.
type Value
  = LiteralValue(LiteralBits)
  | RecordValue(List<NamedField>)
  | VariantValue { tag: DeclarationId, payload: Value }
  | NodeRef(NodeId)
  | CardinalityValue(LoopBound)

// 🟡 SCAFFOLD at PR-B.2 observation-carrier scope. Comparable program
// observations are producer-neutral: Rust emit+build+run and eager DAG eval
// both target this same envelope, and neither lineage owns the carrier. The
// generic `Carrier` is the typed observation domain; value-output differential
// claims use `ProgramObservation<Value>`, while later lineages may introduce
// other typed carriers without adding parallel observation records. This shape
// intentionally carries only the observed value, not stdout/stderr strings,
// exit status, target language, or evaluator strategy. Those are producer
// evidence and diagnostics, not the comparable observation itself.
// Dissolution trigger: PR-B.2 W1/W3 lands the first declared
// `ProgramObservation<Value>` consumer/producer path for `DifferentialEquals`;
// then this carrier graduates to terminal observation-envelope authority.
type ProgramObservation<Carrier> {
  observed: Carrier
}

// 🟢 TERMINAL at PR-A.2 evaluator-state scope. Per
// docs/briefs/r2-pr-a-runtime-value-model.md §Substrate Targets and
// docs/design-pb-runtime-interpreter.md §3.3, closed-over environments are
// evaluator-internal state, not observable `Value` inhabitants. `EvalFrame`
// is one binding scope: a finite partial function from `PortId` to runtime
// `Value`. `Map<PortId, Value>` (= `PartialFunction<PortId, Value>` per
// `dsl/std/types.dag:213`) makes duplicate binding for one `PortId`
// unrepresentable at the carrier boundary; this is the locked shape and
// must not be replaced with a duplicate-admitting `List<EvalBinding>`.
type EvalFrame {
  bindings: Map<PortId, Value>
}

// 🟢 TERMINAL at PR-A.2 evaluator-state scope. Stack of `EvalFrame`s for
// nested calls, branch path bindings, and bounded loop iterations, locked
// to `List<EvalFrame>` by `docs/briefs/r2-pr-a-runtime-value-model.md`
// §Substrate Targets and the merged audit
// `docs/briefs/r2-pr-a-2-eval-frame-dependency-audit.md`. Frame push/pop
// is evaluator-internal; the stack is not observable as a `Value`. PR-A.3
// consumes this stack structurally through `EvalStateKey` / `EvalMemoKey`;
// PR-A.2 must not silently amend the locked carrier shape.
type EvalStateStack {
  frames: List<EvalFrame>
}

// 🟢 TERMINAL at PR-A.3 memo-key scope. Memoization identity is structural:
// the reachable evaluator state is the `EvalStateStack`, not a string digest,
// declaration name, frame count, or other name-only fingerprint. A future
// digest carrier may replace this only when its construction and equality are
// declared as the single authority over reachable-state identity.
type EvalStateKey {
  state: EvalStateStack
}

// 🟢 TERMINAL at PR-A.3 eager-baseline scope. The evaluator's first executable
// strategy is applicative/eager evaluation, and this carrier intentionally has
// exactly one inhabitant until a later slice lands another executable strategy
// with its evaluation rule, memo-key inclusion, and TC2 obligation. Do not add
// `NormalOrder`, `RightFirst`, or parallel evaluation variants as placeholders.
type EvalStrategy = ApplicativeOrder { input_order: InputEvaluationOrder }

// 🟢 TERMINAL at PR-A.3 eager-baseline scope. `LeftFirst` is the only input
// order consumed by the initial evaluator strategy. Additional order variants
// are semantic expansions and must land with executable evaluator behavior.
type InputEvaluationOrder = LeftFirst

// 🟢 TERMINAL at PR-A.3 memo-key scope. This declares the key shape for any
// later evaluator memo table without implementing caching behavior. `state_key`
// is structural evaluator state and `strategy` is the closed strategy carrier;
// neither may be replaced by strings, names, or host-only labels.
type EvalMemoKey {
  program: DeclarationId
  node: NodeId
  state_key: EvalStateKey
  strategy: EvalStrategy
}

// 🟡 SCAFFOLD at PB-Runtime Item-4 structural-landing scope. The canonical
// PB-Runtime entry-point signature locked by
// `docs/design-pb-runtime-interpreter.md` §3.2 lines 80-103. Per PB Manager
// disposition for tracker #2227 (#2074 c#4410581189 + c#4410646513), sub-gates
// 1+2 (`lens_apply_dot_rs_retired`, `lens_testgen_dot_rs_retired`) close on
// the **signature** landing structurally; the per-`Behavior` evaluation rules
// are authority of the design doc (referenced verbatim below) and are NOT
// authored as DSL fn body in this slice. The body is a stub literal
// placeholder so the signature lowers cleanly.
//
// Co-located with the `Value` / `EvalFrame` / `EvalStateStack` carriers above
// per refined-(I) disposition (#2074 c#4410646513): single-authority for the
// `v3.std.runtime` module. The original Q1 path `dsl/std/runtime/runtime.dag`
// was advisory and unreachable by the bootstrap loader at HEAD
// (`src/v3/compiler/build.rs:389` collects `src/v3/std/*.dag` non-recursively;
// `dsl_std_dir` is `rerun-if-changed` only). PB Mgr is updating Q1 wording
// post-merge.
//
// Per-`Behavior` evaluation rules (design-doc §3.2 lines 96-103, verbatim
// reference, NOT DSL-authored in this slice):
//
//   - `Behavior::Value(v)` → emit `LiteralValue(v.payload)`.
//   - `Behavior::Transform(t)` → recursive evaluate `t.inputs`; apply
//     `t.target` to result. Per `t.target` variant:
//       - `Callable(decl_id)` → resolve `decl_id`'s declared Arrow type;
//         on `ArrowBody::UserDefined(body_node_id)`, bind `t.inputs` to the
//         function's declared parameters in a fresh evaluation frame
//         (§3.3); evaluate `body_node_id` in that frame; the frame pops
//         when the call returns. Other `ArrowBody` variants are
//         non-evaluable (`ExternalRealization` dispatches to host;
//         `Pending` / `NoBody` / `Unparsed` are evaluation-time errors).
//       - `FieldProject { field_label, field_child }` → project
//         `field_label` from the (single-input) record value.
//       - `Operator(op_kind)` → apply the primitive operator to inputs.
//   - `Behavior::Branch(b)` → evaluate `b.input`; pattern-match against
//     `b.paths`; recursive evaluate the selected `path.body` with
//     `path.binding` bound in a fresh frame.
//   - `Behavior::Loop(l)` → fold over `l.bound` (cardinality bounded
//     iteration or descent-bounded recursion per the `LoopBound`
//     coproduct); evaluate `l.body` per iteration with accumulator bound
//     to `l.init`'s value initially, threaded through subsequent
//     iterations.
//   - `Behavior::Bind(b)` → register `b.name` as resolvable; the value
//     reachable through `b.result_port` becomes the bound value. Does NOT
//     execute a body — the body that uses the bound name lives at
//     downstream Transform/Bind nodes.
//
// Scope discipline (per #2227 + #2074 c#4410581189):
//   - The fixture-local `pb_runtime_evaluate` at
//     `src/v3/compiler/tests/fixtures/r3_pb_runtime_evaluator_corpus_seeds.dag`
//     and the load-bearing Row-4 ratchet at
//     `src/v3/compiler/tests/integration/r3_pb_runtime_evaluator_corpus_seed_test.rs:77`
//     STAY untouched: real-producer wiring is a separate downstream
//     coordination slice post-R2-Evaluator Rust `evaluate` per design-doc
//     §5.3 (Evaluator Mgr lane authority).
//
// Dissolution trigger: the stub body dissolves when the downstream
// coordination slice replaces it with the per-`Behavior` fold body
// authored against R2-Evaluator's PR-A through PR-E landings. At that
// point the Row-4 ratchet retires per design-doc §5.1 sub-gate 3
// (`regen_lens_dot_rs_retired`, gated on Items 4+5).
fn evaluate(program: Dag, entry: NodeId, args: List<Value>) -> Value =
  LiteralValue(LitInt(0))
